{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "The Look of Your Buttons",
  "summary": "Line buttons up, show their names, make them text or square, and outline a region instead of filling it.",
  "order": 7,
  "practice": "../_scenes/arm_toggle.blend",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1: Line Them Up",
      "text": [
        "1. In the Kneady tab, click Forearm in the tree.",
        "2. Under Its Buttons, click Column.",
        "3. Hover the forearm: its buttons stand one above the other.",
        "",
        "The arm is as Toggles and Show When left it: FK switches it, and Bend or Reach shows. Row, Column, Row + Column and Circle line a region's buttons up in its middle."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "01_column.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].arrange"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].arrange",
          "is": "COLUMN"
        },
        {
          "hovered": "Forearm",
          "object": "Arm"
        }
      ],
      "start": {
        "mode": "OBJECT",
        "select": [
          "Arm"
        ],
        "active": "Arm",
        "sidebar": "Kneady",
        "view": {
          "location": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            0.0
          ],
          "rotation": [
            0.71238,
            0.44106,
            0.28736,
            0.46412
          ],
          "distance": 2.4,
          "perspective": "PERSP"
        },
        "set": [
          {
            "path": "scene.kneady_on",
            "value": true
          },
          {
            "path": "scene.kneady_labels",
            "value": "HOVER"
          },
          {
            "path": "scene.kneady_highlight",
            "value": "FILL"
          },
          {
            "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].tree_open",
            "value": false
          },
          {
            "path": "window_manager.kneady_row",
            "value": -1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2: Show Their Names",
      "text": [
        "1. At the top of the Kneady tab, set Labels to Always.",
        "2. Hover the forearm: every button's name shows.",
        "",
        "On Hover shows the name of the button under the mouse only; Off shows none. This setting is for all of Kneady."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "02_labels.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "scene.kneady_labels"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "scene.kneady_labels",
          "is": "ALWAYS"
        },
        {
          "hovered": "Forearm",
          "object": "Arm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3: A Text Button",
      "text": [
        "1. Click the arrow beside Forearm in the tree, then click FK.",
        "2. Set its Icon to Text.",
        "",
        "A text button shows its name in its box, instead of arrows: good for a switch."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "03_text.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[2].icon_type"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[2].icon_type",
          "is": "TEXT"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4: Square Buttons",
      "text": [
        "1. Click Bend in the tree, and click Square.",
        "2. Do the same for Reach.",
        "",
        "A shape tells kinds of button apart at a glance: here the drag buttons are square, and the switch is text."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "04_square.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[0].shape",
        "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[1].shape"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[0].shape",
          "is": "SQUARE"
        },
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[1].shape",
          "is": "SQUARE"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5: Outline Instead of Fill",
      "text": [
        "1. At the top of the Kneady tab, set Highlight to Outline.",
        "2. Hover the forearm: the region shows as its outline, in its color.",
        "",
        "Outline keeps the mesh in view while you work. Outline Width, under it, sets how thick it is."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "05_outline.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "scene.kneady_highlight"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "scene.kneady_highlight",
          "is": "OUTLINE"
        },
        {
          "hovered": "Forearm",
          "object": "Arm"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
